INT. COURTHOUSE STAIRWELL - DAY

Concrete steps. A buzzing light. Muffled voices from above.

ATTORNEY NADIA FAROUQ, forties, stands against the wall with a briefcase. Her client, DARRELL OKAFOR, thirty, stands one step below, suit too big at the shoulders.

NADIA
Say the date again.

DARRELL
March fourth.

NADIA
And the time.

DARRELL
Nine-fifteen.

She nods. She straightens his tie. He lets her. His hand is steady. Hers is not. She puts it in her pocket.

NADIA
If they ask about the knife.

DARRELL
I never saw a knife.

NADIA
Good.

Above them a door opens and closes. She picks up her briefcase and goes up one step. He doesn't move.

DARRELL
You believe me?

NADIA
I believe the record.

She goes up another step. He follows.
